Description: FortiOS MCP server for AI clients
 forti-mcp lets an AI client (Claude Code, Codex or any other MCP client)
 discover, read and change FortiGate configuration through the FortiOS REST
 API (v2), and never through SSH or CLI commands. The client starts it on
 demand and talks to it over stdio (JSON-RPC 2.0); there is no daemon and no
 network listener.
 .
 Changes are planned first: a plan validates the operations and records the
 field diff and risk tier. Whether a plan may be applied is the device
 profile's mode (read-only, guarded or autonomous), which the operator sets
 and the server cannot change.
 .
 Device profiles and credentials are managed with `forti configure` from the
 forti-cli package, which also registers the server with AI clients
 (`forti install mcp`). forti-mcp itself needs neither: the command engine it
 shares with forti is compiled in.
